Rules: Discovery

Purpose:
  Defines discovery engine rules and principles.

Principles:
  SOURCE CODE:
    ↓
  OBSERVE:
    ↓
  INFER:
    ↓
  VALIDATE:
    ↓
  MODEL:

FactClassification:
  FACT:
    Directly proven from source code
  INFERRED:
    Logical conclusion from source code
  UNKNOWN:
    No information available
  CONFLICT:
    .sdd differs from source

DiscoveryModes:
  GREENFIELD:
    New project from business input
  BROWNFIELD:
    Existing project from source code
  HYBRID:
    Existing project with new requirements

AnalysisScope:
  Structure:
    Directory layout, module organization
  Stack:
    Languages, frameworks, runtimes
  Architecture:
    Patterns, layers, dependencies
  Domains:
    Business domains, boundaries
  Testing:
    Test types, frameworks, coverage
  Security:
    Authentication, authorization, gaps
  Infrastructure:
    Deployment, environments, cloud
  Documentation:
    Existing docs, gaps
  Workflow:
    CI/CD, pipelines

QualityGate:
  DISCOVERY COMPLETE requires:
    - Structure known
    - Stack known
    - Architecture sufficiently known
    - Critical dependencies known
    - Security baseline known
    - Testing baseline known

DiscoveryRules:
  [DR1]  Discovery MUST analyze, not modify source code.
  [DR2]  Discovery MUST classify all findings.
  [DR3]  Discovery MUST assign confidence to inferences.
  [DR4]  Discovery MUST detect drift between .sdd and source.
  [DR5]  Discovery MUST produce actionable backlog.
  [DR6]  Discovery MUST create baseline for future comparison.
  [DR7]  Discovery MUST detect circular dependencies.
  [DR8]  Discovery MUST identify security gaps.

State: +
  